        "symptom": "/og-edge/hosted and /og-edge/edge returned 200 image/png 1200x630, but both were the same solid #064e3b card with no text: identical ETag (062b3cea...c478) and image entropy 0.000. verify-url's format, dimension, and content-type checks alone would have accepted them. The CDN cached both for 24h under Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, so those slugs are not used as evidence.",
        "diagnosis": "Diagnostic deploy 6ae7a13742402c1143a1acf1 logged every asset fetch: two fresh cold-start slugs rendered text (entropy 0.215 and 0.213), and /wasm/layout.wasm (200 application/wasm, 520763 bytes, head 0061736d), /wasm/resvg.wasm (200 application/wasm, 2478606 bytes, head 0061736d), and /fonts/inter-latin-700-normal.woff (200 application/font-woff, 31320 bytes, head 774f4646) all returned the right bytes. A local Node reproduction of createEdgeOg with the same files renders text on the first call, sequential and concurrent. Most likely a first-deploy propagation race: the same-origin font fetch received non-font bytes while the brand-new site propagated, and Satori drew no glyphs without raising an error. Not reproduced on demand.",
